<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 1 April, from 527 to 1976.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">527 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,499 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justin I makes his nephew Justinian co-emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The ageing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justin-i">Justin I</a> raised Justinian to co-emperor of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. Within months he ruled alone, and his reign would reconquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, codify <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> and raise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagia-sophia">Hagia Sophia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justin-i">Justin I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1572">1572 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">454 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sea Beggars capture Brielle from Spain</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rebel privateers known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-beggars">Sea Beggars</a> seized the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brielle">Brielle</a>. It was the revolt's first secure foothold on land and set off a wave of risings across Holland and Zeeland against Spanish rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1865">1865 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sheridan breaks the Confederate line at Five Forks</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Union troops under Philip Sheridan routed Confederates at Five Forks, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, cutting Lee's last supply railway into Petersburg. Lee abandoned Petersburg and Richmond the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Royal Air Force formed as the first independent air force</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> merged the Royal Flying Corps and the Royal Naval Air Service into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-air-force">Royal Air Force</a>, the world's first air arm independent of army and navy control.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1924">1924 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">102 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Munich court sentences Hitler to five years for the Beer Hall Putsch</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> received five years' detention for his failed coup of November 1923. He served barely nine months at Landsberg, where he dictated Mein Kampf.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nazi regime stages a nationwide boycott of Jewish businesses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">SA men stood outside Jewish-owned shops, offices and surgeries across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> to turn customers away. The one-day boycott was the first nationally coordinated anti-Jewish action of the new regime.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1939">1939 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Franco declares the Spanish Civil War over</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the last Republican forces surrendered, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-franco">Francisco Franco</a> announced the end of the war. His victory began a dictatorship that would last until his death in 1975.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US forces land on Okinawa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American troops came ashore on Okinawa in Operation Iceberg, the largest amphibious assault of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a>. The 82-day battle that followed cost the lives of well over 100,000 soldiers and civilians.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-war">Pacific War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1976">1976 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">50 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jobs, Wozniak and Wayne found Apple Computer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak and Ronald Wayne signed the partnership that created Apple Computer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Its first product was the hand-built Apple I; Wayne sold his share within days.</p></div></li></ol>
