<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 1 April <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eleanor-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eleanor of Aquitaine</span><span class="tp">c. 1122–1204</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/aimery-of-cyprus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aimery-of-cyprus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Aimery of Cyprus</span><span class="tp">d. 1205</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/abaqa-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/abaqa-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Abaqa Khan</span><span class="tp">1234–1282</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nuno-alvares-pereira"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nuno-alvares-pereira.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nuno Álvares Pereira</span><span class="tp">1360–1431</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/blanche-i-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/blanche-i-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Blanche I of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1387–1441</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-i-the-old"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-i-the-old.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sigismund I the Old</span><span class="tp">1467–1548</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/george-ii-of-greece"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/george-ii-of-greece.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">George II of Greece</span><span class="tp">1890–1947</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
